{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1418137-quintessence-quarry-extracting-from-matter-coincidentally","id":1418137,"title":"Quintessence Quarry: extracting from matter, coincidentally.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-10-13T21:03:29-07:00","id":1418137,"title":"Quintessence Quarry: extracting from matter, coincidentally.","content":"(Question at the end.)<br /> <br /> I have a storyteller-played support character for a chronicle with two other players. He is the workshop guy, a Son of Ether with Prime 3 and Matter 3 who creates body armor, spy gadgets and other necessities of an adventurous Tradition Cabal. We are playing without the &quot;affinity sphere must always be highest&quot; limitation. The point of taking the Prime Sphere is that I don't want my players to have to worry about not having this meta-Sphere or having to face a metaphysical learning curve in their first time playing. They can take the Spheres that actually do stuff and when I get Prime 4, we can obtain quintessence from matter. So, seeing as the Etherites have the whole Hollow Earth mythology, I thought I would be a mechanical engineer, able to create mining robots. Assuming we can buy some land and get a mining permit, I have a repeatable cycle of Magickal effects that I believe would be coincidental. <br /> <br /> 1. Bring a caterpillar and ore truck. Build a workshop for assembling mining robots. Buy any components for a mining robot that have electrical charge or chemical instability, since I don't have Forces. The workshop hides what is happening inside and presumably makes the next step coincidental.<br /> 2. Instantiate a mining robot using Prime 2, Matter 3. Bring the robot out into plain view, supporting the next coincidence.<br /> 3. Extract a section of rock for quintessence using Matter 3, Prime 4, to be shared with the Cabal (the non-monetary payoff).<br /> 4. Instantiate ore in the truck's bin of the same composition as the extracted rock, which I scanned with Matter 1. Drive to the ore processing plant and sell it (the financial payoff that also lets me hold onto the quarry). <br /> 5. Buy more Forces-necessary parts for the next mining robot, head back and instantiate another mining robot. Extract a bigger hole. Rinse and repeat. <br /> <br /> As a storyteller, would this work in your chronicle?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-13T21:58:06-07:00","id":1418142,"title":"","content":"Yeah I'd allow it. Something like that might get a rival's attention. As it would require near constant maintenance in exchange for several backgrounds it might also become an interesting plot point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26088-actual_table","name":"Actual_Table","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26088_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-14T05:17:41-07:00","id":1418175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1418137-quintessence-quarry-extracting-from-matter-coincidentally#post1418137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We are playing without the &quot;affinity sphere must always be highest&quot; limitation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tangent 1: Huh? The only rule about your Affinity Sphere is that you have to have at least one dot in it. You don't have to have it as your highest.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The point of taking the Prime Sphere is that I don't want my players to have to worry about not having this meta-Sphere or having to face a metaphysical learning curve in their first time playing. </div> </div> </div>Tangent 2: IME, it's best to learn Mage by actually playing with the full rules. The fastest way to learn the way the Spheres work is to use them, and discouraging the players from taking Prime is very odd to me considering how important the first few dots are to most concepts; there's a lot of &quot;actually do stuff&quot; in there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, seeing as the Etherites have the whole Hollow Earth mythology,... </div> </div> </div>Tangent 3: Some do, some don't. Though all Etherites acknowledge that the Consensus Earth most people exist in most of the time doesn't have a Hollow Earth and their ability to go to one (of possibly many) is part of the wackiness of Ether Science!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The workshop hides what is happening inside and presumably makes the next step coincidental. </div> </div> </div>Simply building a workshop around something doesn't make it coincidental, it just makes it vulgar without witnesses. You have to turn it into a full Sanctum to even start to get to the point of possibly making it coincidental.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. Instantiate a mining robot using Prime 2, Matter 3. Bring the robot out into plain view, supporting the next coincidence. </div> </div> </div>I... don't think instantiate is the word you're looking for. Though that aside, you also need Matter 4 to create a complex machines out of nothing but raw magical energy. And that's assuming a relatively simple machine like an everyday industrial robot that simply follows instructions given to it and doesn't really do much in the way of thinking. Which means you're going to either have to operate the robot, or add even more magic to make it better than current technology so it can replicate what miners + robots can do now.<br /> <br /> In any case, without a Sanctum and without the Etherite having a Focus that supports this effect, it's going to be vulgar without witnesses. Robots don't just appear out of thin air, and Etherits as technomages are generally going to not have Focuses that promote such things... they'd at least have a fancy 3D printer or something technologically inclined of that nature as an Instrument for this. Even if the Sanctum and Focus is there, the robot needs to conform to what robots are capable of doing or it risks destroying itself from Pattern Bleed. Alternately it's a Wonder or Familiar with plenty of problems along the same lines. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3. Extract a section of rock for quintessence using Matter 3, Prime 4, to be shared with the Cabal (the non-monetary payoff). </div> </div> </div>How much quintessence are you imagining comes out of a rock you just pulled out of the ground to justify all this?<br /> <br /> If you have Prime 4... it seems like finding and tapping Wellsprings will be a much more useful endeavor.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 4. Instantiate ore in the truck's bin of the same composition as the extracted rock, which I scanned with Matter 1. Drive to the ore processing plant and sell it (the financial payoff that also lets me hold onto the quarry). </div> </div> </div>That's not how this works. All the quintessence you'd get from destroying it would need to be put back in to remake it (or come from somewhere else and you could have just taken if from there). Rocks aren't inherently full of extra magical power such that you can destroy and rebuild them and get a rock and magical power out of the equation. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As a storyteller, would this work in your chronicle? </div> </div> </div>Not particularly.<br /> <br /> The only way this would be remotely plausible in my game would be if there's a Node underground, and the mining operation is extracting Tass in the form of ore, and then taking the excess quintessence from the tass as part of the processing of the ore so it leaves as normal old rock. Which also completely removes the need for 99% of this because you only need to add one step to a normal mining operation. You don't need magical robots and full destruction/reconstruction level effects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-14T07:03:23-07:00","id":1418185,"title":"","content":"Seems like a lot of work for very little reward, but plausible.<br /> <br /> The main issue is going to be the incredibly noticable lack of waste. Normally quarry's and mines have waste stone piles. They do stuff with that stone. People are going to approach you wanting to buy it for driveways, gardens, etc.<br /> <br /> You're just erasing it from existence and pocketing the magical energy.<br /> <br /> Also Heavy Arms, I took his mean to be 'erase the stone, leave the ore.' so he gets tass from the stone, and then still has ore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-14T10:26:41-07:00","id":1418211,"title":"","content":"I obviously didn't get that from part 4 (why would you need magic to get material in the the truck if you already separated out the ore from the rest?).<br /> <br /> To me though, that just makes it worse because &quot;lower quality&quot; Matter means less quintessence per volume; however a given Paradigm explains the way quintessence mirrors value. It does get rid of the &quot;spend what you got to remake the rock,&quot; part of my objection, but you've still got the making a magical robot issue that's probably going to eat up all the quintessence you could get out of destroying tons of dirt and gravel. The ore that's valuable enough to ship and sell is the part that has any real value in quintessence depending on what's in it. And the scenario didn't include any of the rock being inherently tass.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-14T10:52:50-07:00","id":1418214,"title":"","content":"Basically his process in so far as I understand it is...<br /> <br /> 1.) Build a mining robot.<br /> 2.) Use the mining robot as cover for why a chunk of the mountainside is just cleanly vaporized into pure magical energy.<br /> 3.) During said vaporizing analyze the chemical makeup of the rock.<br /> 4.) Reconstitute the valuable ore from the raw magical energy.<br /> <br /> Rinse repeat.<br /> <br /> Personally, this seems like a situation where you could get away with just hiring a mining crew and taking off with a truckload of waste stone every night.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-14T12:37:51-07:00","id":1418231,"title":"","content":"Or... I don't know.... be a defector from the Syndicate and still have Primal Utility so you can just run a normal company without all of these probably vulgar effects to get a trickle of quintessence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-15T01:18:21-07:00","id":1418314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1418137-quintessence-quarry-extracting-from-matter-coincidentally?p=1418231#post1418231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or... I don't know.... be a defector from the Syndicate and still have Primal Utility so you can just run a normal company without all of these probably vulgar effects to get a trickle of quintessence.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is a good idea. Unfortunately, I'm too advanced in the chronicle to change my backstory. I revealed some of it in dialogue. Primal Utility is an amazing tech-Sphere. The Technocracy on Earth is supposed to suffer from being Spirit-blind, the Void Engineers often being absent from the Earthly setting. In the Avatar Storm metaplot, the Void Engineers are grounded and they are teaching NWO Operatives DS to prepare for the housecleaning needed to remove Wyrm infestation (the problem of which doesn't improve the Traditions' position at all). So, the Technocracy has all nine Spheres + Primal Utility. The Technocratic paradigm advantages them, with Paradox punishing the Traditions. It illustrates the absurdity I face in running a Tradition campaign. In creating my setting, I went with the following assumptions.<br /> <br /> 1. The Technocracy controls the most powerful Nodes in the region. <br /> <br /> 2. The Nodes usable by the Traditions are already controlled by members of a Chantry the players don't know exists yet (even when being initiated into the Verbena, one character sees the other attendees faces blurred by a Forces effect, in case she is captured). They haven't gotten to the point of having the time and energy to do membership-worthy missions for the main mentor-NPC connected to this chantry. <br /> <br /> 3. There are no unclaimed nodes or wellsprings, because any Mage with Correspondence 2 and Prime 1 can find such a resource, alert his Cabal/ Symposium and fortify the location. The Technocracy has the force advantage needed to stake most claims.<br /> <br /> 4. Players split their seven background points between Avatar and Arcane. The idea behind emphasizing Arcane is they get a grace period before the Technocracy becomes aware of their existence and they are a little bit harder to find, even if they make newbie mistakes (like using Tim Hortons as a meeting place and sitting under ball-cameras).<br /> <br /> 5. The Prime Sphere, combined with any one of the other three Pattern Spheres can be used to obtain Quintessence. Extracting Quintessence from Life is a wee bit Nephandic. <br /> <br /> 6. A Cabal is best served with individual Mages each focusing on raising a single Sphere as high as possible, four or five, to begin with. This raises the difficulty of Magick roles, particularly when facing conflict in which extreme coincidences follow each other.<br /> <br /> 7. Being the Mage who obtains Quintessence is boring. I want them to have fun playing their characters. <br /> <br /> 8. Most of the missions they undertake will require them to travel. Even if they had a Node (and small Nodes don't provide enough for a Cabal to do much or very often), they will often be away from their home base.<br /> <br /> I watched a chronicle that was posted on YouTube. The storyteller had some good ideas and was able to handle things on the fly. The players had original character concepts. They had a Sanctum. They mostly stayed home. Investigations were done by internet. I decided I didn't want my chronicle to be about staying in the safe place. One of the five session-xp criteria is danger (reasonably balanced to their power and limited player experience at using Magick). So, I made a character who could obtain quintessence, putting everything into fulfilling this role, in accordance with the rules, as I understand them. I eventually want the chronicle to be something that can be written and shared with other storytellers. The conclusion I have come to is that the Prime Sphere is BS when it comes to obtaining quintessence as a lowly starting Mage. <br /> <br /> Fortunately, we haven't gotten to the point where I build the quarrying facility, because we have no money. So, I haven't done anything that would make the story incompatible with common interpretations of the rules.<br /> <br /> Heavy Arms &quot;Tangent 2: IME, it's best to learn Mage by actually playing with the full rules. The fastest way to learn the way the Spheres work is to use them, and discouraging the players from taking Prime is very odd to me considering how important the first few dots are to most concepts; there's a lot of &quot;actually do stuff&quot; in there.&quot;<br /> <br /> My first player, my girlfriend, picked her two favorite Spheres first. The other player focused on building a character using a longstanding existing concept of his, not concerning himself with Spheres. He left me to pick his Mentor's Tradition and the Spheres the mentor could teach. I reveal things about Prime and Quintessence through my character's dialogue. <br /> <br /> Heavy Arms &quot;Simply building a workshop around something doesn't make it coincidental, it just makes it vulgar without witnesses. You have to turn it into a full Sanctum to even start to get to the point of possibly making it coincidental.&quot;<br /> <br /> How Do You Do That, p45, right column, under heading: Conjuring Material Forms,<br /> &quot;For obvious reasons, this sort of thing tends to be vulgar Magick, although a sufficient level of concealment can make it seem coincidental.&quot; It then refers to the Axis of Coincidence chart M20,p533-534, which emphasizes Hypothetical Average Bystander (HAB) and Process Based Determinism (PBD). What would the average person believe? How do you do it?<br /> <br /> For comparison, I'll just use the example of someone I knew who had Crones and Fibromyalgia. She had a hard time getting out of bed. She had not put out her garbage in some time and was afraid that if she took it all out in one day, everyone in her building would know how much had accumulated. So, I explained why this was not such a big deal. On any individual trip, there is a good chance that one of the apartment dwellers whose window faces the dumpster will see, because people watching TV or considering going outside occasionally look out the window. With repeated trips, the number of individual observers will tend to increase, even to the point of everyone having seen her do a single trip. However, it is unlikely anyone would note the exact time they saw her take out the garbage or go knocking on neighbors' doors to compare sightings. Each person witnessed a normal event happen (HAB). The process she used took time to move a hidden quantity of Matter without drawing attention to herself (PBR).<br /> <br /> My quarry would be in a remote place with access to a highway. If all the drivers passing by organized by cell phone to meet and compare what they saw passing by, I would be screwed - highly unlikely. I am using a process that hides the totality of what I'm doing from any individual HAB.<br /> <br /> Heavy Arms &quot;I... don't think instantiate is the word you're looking for. &quot;<br /> <br /> I took it from computer programming when I was learning to use a game modding tool. I mean &quot;create out of nothing&quot;.<br /> <br /> Heavy Arms &quot;Though that aside, you also need Matter 4 to create a complex machines out of nothing but raw magical energy.&quot;<br /> <br /> Piece by piece it is.<br /> <br /> &quot;And that's assuming a relatively simple machine like an everyday industrial robot that simply follows instructions given to it and doesn't really do much in the way of thinking. Which means you're going to either have to operate the robot, or add even more magic to make it better than current technology so it can replicate what miners + robots can do now.&quot;<br /> <br /> Robots are controlled by computers. Fruit-picking robots use cameras to understand their environment and reach for the ripe fruit, wherever it's hanging. Mining robots use ground penetrating radar to keep track of the task they are performing. There are companies that sell complete, automated mining packages to rich investors. I actually watched a promotional video emphasizing the near total elimination of labor costs. <br /> <br /> &quot;That's not how this works. All the quintessence you'd get from destroying it would need to be put back in to remake it (or come from somewhere else and you could have just taken if from there). Rocks aren't inherently full of extra magical power such that you can destroy and rebuild them and get a rock and magical power out of the equation.&quot;<br /> <br /> How much mass/ volume/ rarity/ value of Matter does one point of quintessence get you? I can't find a conversion chart anywhere. Nowhere do the books specify a cost for Fuel Pattern. I had always understood from years of play with experienced storytellers that if you use Prime 2 to fuel a new pattern, the Quintessence comes from the tellurian. Considering you are not supposed to go above 5 in a Sphere, using Prime 4 to extract from Matter should keep a Cabal supplied with quintessence until Prime 5, whereupon I create a Node. It's so ridiculous when the main function of the Sphere is getting and redirecting Quintessence. 1 - Can't do anything. 2 - Still nothing. 3 - No. 4 - Something, we're not sure how much. 5- And now ultimate power.<br /> <br /> Using Prime's other powers:<br /> Tired of surviving on conjured Ramen noodles, Draven took the change in his pocket, went to the hardware store and bought himself a brand new pickaxe. He spent the rest of the day enchanting it until it could cut through the hardest rock with ease. Now, if he could only convince his friend, a Life Mage who revered Gaia, to attack an ore vein with Magickal might. He would get this vision realized if it meant starting out with the crudest methods. &quot;One day.&quot;, he said determinedly, &quot;One day.&quot;. <br /> <br /> I will adapt my character's Process and improve the roleplaying to show players how Prime works on a simple mechanical level and how one progresses through the Sphere.<br /> <br /> Happy Gaming! <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-15T04:51:18-07:00","id":1418342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1418137-quintessence-quarry-extracting-from-matter-coincidentally?p=1418314#post1418314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. The Nodes usable by the Traditions are already controlled by members of a Chantry the players don't know exists yet (even when being initiated into the Verbena, one character sees the other attendees faces blurred by a Forces effect, in case she is captured). They haven't gotten to the point of having the time and energy to do membership-worthy missions for the main mentor-NPC connected to this chantry.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your setup is... well... a Quintessence limited one. What's the point of setting up a situation where the PCs are light on quintessence and then try to get them a source of their own instead of letting it push them to pursue membership?<br /> <br /> I'd look into the Chantry using tass as payments for tasks the PCs/associated NPCs do on the Chantry's behalf that aren't big enough to earn membership (though... that's a fairly extreme position in and of itself... Tradition mages are in an alliance with each other, keeping other Tradition mages out in the cold isn't really condusive towards maintaining that alliance).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3. There are no unclaimed nodes or wellsprings,... </div> </div> </div>Nobody can really claim Wellsprings. That's one of their bigger appeals. As transitory events they happen when they happen - sometimes once, sometimes according to difficult to decipher occult formulas, sometimes semi-reliably - whichever mages are there at the right time with enough Prime can tap into it and there's really nothing any other mages can do about it. If you could claim it, it would be a Juncture not a Wellspring (and even those are hard to claim practically).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 5. The Prime Sphere, combined with any one of the other three Pattern Spheres can be used to obtain Quintessence. Extracting Quintessence from Life is a wee bit Nephandic. </div> </div> </div>It's not that you can't destroy things for quintessence, it's just generally vulgar to do so and most patterns don't actually contain much to begin with. Mages don't bother with these sorts of schemes because it's a hug amount of effort for what's likely to just amount to 4-5 quintessence a year. If you're not going to just use the sacrificing rules (but then you need to sacrifice something of value, or it's not really a sacrifice), and going the full &quot;destroy it by removing all it's quintessence&quot; route, you're not going to get a lot out of the effort.<br /> <br /> And while it might seem a bit Nephandic to some, animal sacrifice is an incredibly common ritual practice for lots of mages. To the Nephandi on the other hand, a mage destroying patterns for quintessence is someone they would look at as a target for corruption or recruitment since they're desperate and willing to consign things to utter destruction for self-interest. They'd much rather target someone that's gotten so desperate they're burning diamonds for quintessence than a Verbena that still does blood sacrifices on holidays according to old rituals.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 6. A Cabal is best served with individual Mages each focusing on raising a single Sphere as high as possible, four or five, to begin with. This raises the difficulty of Magick roles, particularly when facing conflict in which extreme coincidences follow each other. </div> </div> </div>I disagree highly.<br /> <br /> First, most bread-and-butter magic is in combining two and three dot Spheres, not in having one Sphere maxed out. While Prime 5 is awesome, it's significantly less so if you don't have at least a decent investment in the Pattern Spheres.<br /> <br /> Second, assuming a Cabal shares enough magical practice to cooperatively cast magic, they all need at least one dot in the effects their Cabal are doing to help out. Group casting is incredibly potent, especially for younger mages that can't get the big dice-pools higher Arete mages with lots of acolytes can get. A Cabal where characters aim for 3 dots in two or three main Spheres, and then one or two dots in all the others will vastly outperform a Cabal where everyone guns for a 4 or 5 ASAP.<br /> <br /> This is even more true with a small Cabal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 7. Being the Mage who obtains Quintessence is boring. I want them to have fun playing their characters. </div> </div> </div>The way the rules are written this isn't really a big deal. Most mages can get a decent amount of quintessence on their own, and a Prime specialist has more to do than this role.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 8. Most of the missions they undertake will require them to travel. Even if they had a Node (and small Nodes don't provide enough for a Cabal to do much or very often), they will often be away from their home base. </div> </div> </div>This... doesn't really sound like a good reason to invest in a very intensive method of getting a trickle of quintessence. If they're traveling a lot.... Tass-as-currency-for-mages is a much better solution to their problems.<br /> <br /> Also, you as the ST dictate how much quintessence a Node mechanically generates according to what you want out of your game. Considering a mage can't even hold more than their Avatar rating in Quintessence without taking Prime 1? They don't exactly need a lot to top up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The conclusion I have come to is that the Prime Sphere is BS when it comes to obtaining quintessence as a lowly starting Mage. </div> </div> </div>Prime 1 lets you convert your own Heath Levels into quintessence if your desperate or have lots of rest time. Prime 2 and 3 allow you to sacrifice things for quintessence.<br /> <br /> The problem here is not the Prime Sphere, the problem is you set up the players with a quintessence access poor local setting, and are trying to dig your way out of it. I'm not trying to be dismissive, but that's the situation you've presented.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It then refers to the Axis of Coincidence chart M20,p533-534, which emphasizes Hypothetical Average Bystander (HAB) and Process Based Determinism (PBD). What would the average person believe? How do you do it? </div> </div> </div>The biggest problem I'm seeing here, is that you're ignoring the H in HAB.<br /> <br /> The Hypothetical Bystander is hypothetical because they're not actually there. It's what that bystander would think if they were in the room with the mage. That's why you can conjure a business card or a small knife coincidentally (a HAB will believe you might have those in your pockets), but not a rocket launcher (because you can't fit that in your pockets). It doesn't matter if you do it away from where average people normally are, as that's negating the H part.<br /> <br /> The HAB is always watching you, just not as closely as the HOO. When your mage ducks into his workshop, the HAB follows. When the robot is created from nothing the HAB disbelieves and it's vulgar w/o witnesses, even if the HAB would be fooled by the workshop into believe in you a simple toy flying drone in one of your mage's cabinets when you actually used magic to create it inside the cabinet, because the HAB would be fooled by your mage rummaging around in a room where it is completely believable random bits of tech might be tucked in a drawer, bin, etc.<br /> <br /> The concealment has to be to the HAB that's standing there theoretically watching you, not to actual people passing by on the highway outside the quarry.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I took it from computer programming when I was learning to use a game modding tool. I mean &quot;create out of nothing&quot;. </div> </div> </div>I figured. Instantiate means to perform or observe a real instance of a hypothetical. Computer programing uses it for when a program's code generates actual processes based on inputs rather than the code sitting there &quot;hypothetically&quot; capable of generating those outputs. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Robots are controlled by computers. Fruit-picking robots use cameras to understand their environment and reach for the ripe fruit, wherever it's hanging. Mining robots use ground penetrating radar to keep track of the task they are performing. There are companies that sell complete, automated mining packages to rich investors. I actually watched a promotional video emphasizing the near total elimination of labor costs. </div> </div> </div>Robots are generally controlled by a mix of computers and biological inputs (I say only because there's some neat cow milking robots that the cows learn to operate instead of having humans do anything).<br /> <br /> Automation is constantly advancing, but we're still pretty far from completely automated work forces. Most &quot;autonomous&quot; mining equipment is more accurately remote controlled mining equipment because there's still an operator or two that get to be safely away from the highly dangerous activity. The robots are still doing a lot of computing on their own to let two operators replace a team of a dozen to two dozen workers, but they're not doing it without human input either.<br /> <br /> More importantly to this scenario: Matter and Prime alone can't generate computer code to have your mining robot programmed as you bring it into existence, and most mining operations use multiple automation based machines, not just one all-purpose mining robot so keeping to modern technology means building lots of different robots, not just one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How much mass/ volume/ rarity/ value of Matter does one point of quintessence get you? </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately left up to the ST rather than having hard rules.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I had always understood from years of play with experienced storytellers that if you use Prime 2 to fuel a new pattern, the Quintessence comes from the tellurian. </div> </div> </div>That presumes someone isn't trying to harvest the free floating quintessence in the local area like your plan relies on. While it is true the default is that there's plenty of free quintessence in the background of reality for mages not to worry about fueling patterns, your plan involves messing with that on a large scale. Also the number of successes you'd need to generate industrial mining amounts of rocks is high enough to get into auto-quintessence costs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Considering you are not supposed to go above 5 in a Sphere, using Prime 4 to extract from Matter should keep a Cabal supplied with quintessence until Prime 5, whereupon I create a Node. </div> </div> </div>Possibly, but the plan you've outlined isn't efficient for this purpose. Matter 2 and Prime 2 will get you lots more Quintessence, but you need objects of significant enough value that destroying them is an actual sacrifice... which means you can't industrialize it... and stealing such objects from Sleepers is a dick move (but hey, lots of mages are assholes). The problems are when you try to turn this into an elaborate scheme that includes an actual front business.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's so ridiculous when the main function of the Sphere is getting and redirecting Quintessence. 1 - Can't do anything. 2 - Still nothing. 3 - No. 4 - Something, we're not sure how much. 5- And now ultimate power. </div> </div> </div>Prime 1: Sense the quintessence in the first place, store more in you than your natural limit, damage yourself for quintessence, redirect quintessence into objects to bind them to your personal Pattern.<br /> Prime 2: Sacrifice objects for quintessence, redirect quintessence into Patterns to fuel them, redirect quintessence into existing objects to make them better.<br /> Prime 3: Sacrifice living things for quintessence, redirect quintessence between willing mages, redirect quintessence into living things to make them better, redirect quintessence directly from some sources to yourself.<br /> <br /> That's not &quot;can't do anything.&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-15T06:54:43-07:00","id":1418356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they're traveling a lot.... Tass-as-currency-for-mages is a much better solution to their problems.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree on everything, but I want to highlight this, because as a traveling mage troupe that want's to &quot;do stuff&quot; (instead of sitting to protect their Quint) this option its not just flat better than any mining opperation (that even if it worked, would require the mages to sit there to avoid their golden goose to get in trouble - as all the people that thought this kinda might work pointed out) but it's also a seed for stories.<br /> <br /> Your mages wan't Quint? Well, <i>other </i>mages have Quint - and they migth be willing to spend it on your mages if they &quot;do stuff&quot; for them. They don't need to be <i>members </i>of any Chantry to get it. Mercenary mages working for Tass it's a classic, and a way to make your players interact with your world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-15T07:39:26-07:00","id":1418361,"title":"","content":"Also, as much as I like the logistics management aspect that can come up in Mage, running an operation like this seems a bit like playing Shadowrun and setting up a factory that makes bulk industrial cleaners and selling that to make money, instead of actually shadowrunning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-15T14:05:21-07:00","id":1418410,"title":"","content":"Well, in due fairness, it's an NPC doing the mining operation rather than the PCs. It's more like a Shadowrunner that's decided to move to being a Mr. Johnson for his ex-team while they're still off being runners.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-16T02:55:48-07:00","id":1418497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1418137-quintessence-quarry-extracting-from-matter-coincidentally?p=1418356#post1418356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree on everything, but I want to highlight this, because as a traveling mage troupe that want's to &quot;do stuff&quot; (instead of sitting to protect their Quint) this option its not just flat better than any mining opperation (that even if it worked, would require the mages to sit there to avoid their golden goose to get in trouble - as all the people that thought this kinda might work pointed out) but it's also a seed for stories.<br /> <br /> Your mages wan't Quint? Well, <i>other </i>mages have Quint - and they migth be willing to spend it on your mages if they &quot;do stuff&quot; for them. They don't need to be <i>members </i>of any Chantry to get it. Mercenary mages working for Tass it's a classic, and a way to make your players interact with your world.</div> </div> </div> </div>They will have the opportunity to do this when their single point of contact deems it safe to introduce them to other Mages from the Chantry. Reasons why this hasn't happened yet are detailed below. A mining operation can be left in charge of a future NPC who lacks financial resources. Also, spent quarries are sometimes filled with water, used to raise fish and support aquaponic farming. Matter would allow suppression of contaminant metal leakage. It is convertible to purposes other Tradition Mages would find appropriate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1418137-quintessence-quarry-extracting-from-matter-coincidentally?p=1418342#post1418342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your setup is... well... a Quintessence limited one. What's the point of setting up a situation where the PCs are light on quintessence and then try to get them a source of their own instead of letting it push them to pursue membership?<br /> <br /> I'd look into the Chantry using tass as payments for tasks the PCs/associated NPCs do on the Chantry's behalf that aren't big enough to earn membership (though... that's a fairly extreme position in and of itself... Tradition mages are in an alliance with each other, keeping other Tradition mages out in the cold isn't really condusive towards maintaining that alliance.</div> </div> </div> </div>My campaigns are different, because I actually have my Tradition NPCs and organizations that have lasted any significant time in Mage's WoD act according to the reality they live in, as it relates to the Technocracy. The Technocracy has the luxury of being able to coordinate large teams in well fortified constructs. It's Conventions and Methodologies serve specialized service and supply roles. Genegineers Supply FACADE who supply Biomechanics and Operatives, for example. When the Union gears up for conflict in a particular area, it first sends front line agents. The Operatives specialize in Mind. M20 nerfed that overpowered Sphere and I nerfed further by giving the player's Avatar the ability to counteract (to a limited degree) coercive/ illusory Procedures used by Operatives. Still, an Operative can hide within line of sight and read a newbie Mage's thoughts.<br /> <br /> If that inexperienced Mage has just been brought into a Chantry, what thoughts are going to be foremost in their mind? All the amazing new friends they just met at this wonderful, Magickal place - wow. Impressions, faces, names, offers, &quot;If you ever need this, I need this.&quot;. A Chantry that admits inexperienced Mages, lets them socialize with everyone and then wander off into the Technocrat's world is going to suffer from a good deal of assassination, if not having its walls battered down. On the other hand, not knowing about the Chantry protects the newbie Mage. If the Operative was unable to obtain intel from a Mind scan, he will likely hang back and wait for the player to become established among the Traditions. The hope is that powerful Chantry members can sweep them away at the right time.<br /> <br /> In my setting, there are three main cities. A government town, where the story started, is strongly influenced by a Tradition Cabal. The Chantry is dispersed over more rural areas and extends into another parts of the county (Correspondence/Spirit gate-linkage). A city whose economy depends on a military contractor is a Technocracy bastion run by ItX time Motion Managers and NWO Ivory Tower. A third city with a mainly commercial economy is contested. The Traditions are able to hold their city, in part because of an unofficial peace agreement between two powerful Mages from the opposed factions. This is enough to deter NPC Mages from outright murdering and kidnapping each other. Spying and minor frame jobs happen from time to time.<br /> <br /> The scarcity theme affects the Technocracy too, sometimes. The players have met one Progenitor Mage who was at the bottom of the rank-hierarchy of a construct and so decided to set up shop in the Tradition city. That Mage has no Node, but is building up a Sanctum. The players chose to tolerate their presence to have some peaceful contact with the opposition. A subplot incentives cooperation, but doesn't bar the players from kidnaping them or killing them, if they decide. In that case, it's a question of how well they cover their tracks.<br /> <br /> How can the Traditions hold their alliance when they leave the newly awakened out in the cold? Players have a single point of contact. Mentors have the first opportunity to shape the new Mage's worldview as they explain the Tradition's Paradigm. As an example, a Verbena Mentor explained that humanity is meant to exist within nature, revere Gaia and accept nature's plenty. Those Progenitors believe nature is meant to be subordinated to human needs. They created GMO agriculture and hormones in milk - yuck! Who would want to work in a lab all day, just to make the world worse? Mentors also routinely explain that the Technocracy may try to poach new recruits. And when the defector joins, they are still viewed as a bit of an RD and are kept in the lower ranks indefinitely. Players can defect to the Technocracy and the campaign caries on. Achieving any status would be a significant challenge, but they would have the comfort of being on the currently-winning side.<br /> <br /> Another reason they have not had the time to do missions is that I put them in the middle of a situation created by Technocratic machinations right from the start. They were not the targets, since it is more of a whole population thing. While they are not on a mission, what they discover will earn them some consideration.<br /> <br /> I follow a rule with regard to Mentors. Even though they a zero-point background, they are not out to deceive the players or sacrifice them. Any other Tradition NPC they encounter afterwards can draw them into nasty situations. So, there will be an opportunity coming up that will give them a chance to consider a dangerous proposal presented by a member of the city-influence Cabal upon approaching them. That could also lead to Tass or Node-access.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1418137-quintessence-quarry-extracting-from-matter-coincidentally?p=1418342#post1418342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nobody can really claim Wellsprings. That's one of their bigger appeals. As transitory events they happen when they happen - sometimes once, sometimes according to difficult to decipher occult formulas, sometimes semi-reliably - whichever mages are there at the right time with enough Prime can tap into it and there's really nothing any other mages can do about it. If you could claim it, it would be a Juncture not a Wellspring (and even those are hard to claim practically).</div> </div> </div> </div>Time 2, Correspondance2, Prime1, depending on the degree to which a given storyteller allows Time to predict future events. I scrapped the book version of casting in conjunction, in favor of a homebrew one that is less restrictive, more balanced and consequential. Mages would not use it very often, because of what it entails. This is the subject of a future post. Forcing players to invest in Spheres they are not interested in with limited xp is punitive.<br /> <br /> Setting-wise, there is a gubernatorial election coming. I have some idea which Mages back which candidates. Could get interesting. Actually, it is a really good idea, because the Traditions could lose influence, but see the PCs get a large supply of quint over a few months. Or the inverse - Traditions win more influence and a tech team goes full Hypertech with the extra quint.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1418137-quintessence-quarry-extracting-from-matter-coincidentally?p=1418342#post1418342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not that you can't destroy things for quintessence, it's just generally vulgar to do so and most patterns don't actually contain much to begin with. Mages don't bother with these sorts of schemes because it's a hug amount of effort for what's likely to just amount to 4-5 quintessence a year. If you're not going to just use the sacrificing rules (but then you need to sacrifice something of value, or it's not really a sacrifice), and going the full &quot;destroy it by removing all it's quintessence&quot; route, you're not going to get a lot out of the effort.<br /> <br /> And while it might seem a bit Nephandic to some, animal sacrifice is an incredibly common ritual practice for lots of mages. To the Nephandi on the other hand, a mage destroying patterns for quintessence is someone they would look at as a target for corruption or recruitment since they're desperate and willing to consign things to utter destruction for self-interest. They'd much rather target someone that's gotten so desperate they're burning diamonds for quintessence than a Verbena that still does blood sacrifices on holidays according to old rituals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which god does an Etherite sacrifice too? Ah - fortunately, I took the Scientific Mystic merit and cosmology 3. Now, to accumulate &quot;treasured&quot; possessions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1418137-quintessence-quarry-extracting-from-matter-coincidentally?p=1418342#post1418342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree highly.<br /> <br /> First, most bread-and-butter magic is in combining two and three dot Spheres, not in having one Sphere maxed out. While Prime 5 is awesome, it's significantly less so if you don't have at least a decent investment in the Pattern Spheres.<br /> <br /> Second, assuming a Cabal shares enough magical practice to cooperatively cast magic, they all need at least one dot in the effects their Cabal are doing to help out. Group casting is incredibly potent, especially for younger mages that can't get the big dice-pools higher Arete mages with lots of acolytes can get. A Cabal where characters aim for 3 dots in two or three main Spheres, and then one or two dots in all the others will vastly outperform a Cabal where everyone guns for a 4 or 5 ASAP.<br /> <br /> <br /> This is even more true with a small Cabal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Two Spheres at three. I encouraged it, rather than force it. If a player wants to have the sensory ability from six different Spheres, they can. It challenges them to use Abilities more often. The Verbena is going for Time 4, which is way better than the equivalent xp in new Spheres. Stop Time and Contingency versus sense this and that.<br /> <br /> I have Prime and Matter. Each player has one of the other Pattern Spheres. Without conjunctional Magick, I can enchant soil nutrients and the Verbena can use a Life3 Time3 effect to make a plant grow and absorb the enchantment. An electromagnetic coil or radio antenna for Forces.<br /> <br /> Again, using homebrew conjunctional magick system.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1418137-quintessence-quarry-extracting-from-matter-coincidentally?p=1418342#post1418342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The way the rules are written this isn't really a big deal. Most mages can get a decent amount of quintessence on their own, and a Prime specialist has more to do than this role.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup. Gonna enchant that pickaxe... or mining drill. I thought of another character concept. Prime 3 Mind 3, blasting patterns to learn from the meta-psychic energy that bounces off.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1418137-quintessence-quarry-extracting-from-matter-coincidentally?p=1418342#post1418342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This... doesn't really sound like a good reason to invest in a very intensive method of getting a trickle of quintessence. If they're traveling a lot.... Tass-as-currency-for-mages is a much better solution to their problems.<br /> <br /> Also, you as the ST dictate how much quintessence a Node mechanically generates according to what you want out of your game. Considering a mage can't even hold more than their Avatar rating in Quintessence without taking Prime 1? They don't exactly need a lot to top up.`</div> </div> </div> </div>There are other reasons for starting a quarry. For me, the way a Node appears and what activity happens there is something to plan and put creative work into. It has to feel special to the players. Not having a reliable source of quintessence for a while makes them appreciate gaining access to one. When I describe it, I want them thinking &quot;Finally, quint.&quot; and &quot;Hey, this place is awesome!&quot; both at the same time. If they are sneaking around near a tech Node, I want it to be imposing and a little alien. Dotting the land with a whole bunch of Nodes would exhaust me and result in a bunch of low-description places that are supposed to be something Unique. Another Syndicate corner office at the top floor. The occult shop.<br /> <br /> As for how much they mechanically generate, I know what feels right. Let's say the average Node is rank 3. The quint from two of these would be enough, over a month, to do the offensive Magick to capture a single Node of the same strength from the Technocracy, making multiple forays to wear down their defensive advantage. I will have to get some dice and do a simulation. It's assuming the same number of Mages on either side. I will just pull templates from the Convention books to run the dice.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1418137-quintessence-quarry-extracting-from-matter-coincidentally?p=1418342#post1418342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Prime 1 lets you convert your own Heath Levels into quintessence if your desperate or have lots of rest time. Prime 2 and 3 allow you to sacrifice things for quintessence.<br /> <br /> The problem here is not the Prime Sphere, the problem is you set up the players with a quintessence access poor local setting, and are trying to dig your way out of it. I'm not trying to be dismissive, but that's the situation you've presented.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that the max Mage to Sleeper ratio is 1/10,000, they will be able to do a lot of Magick on Sleepers and the environment that doesn't require quint expenditure. This will yield influence that can be leveraged for starting projects like the quarry. We are more likely to do something large scale that is one of the player's ideas first.<br /> <br /> Come to think of it, a concert could produce a Wellspring. One character has Artistically Gifted and Enchanted Voice, related to singing. She is having a second identity crafted for her by her Mentor's allies that she can use when doing low-key activities. (They're not completely out in the cold)<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1418137-quintessence-quarry-extracting-from-matter-coincidentally?p=1418342#post1418342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The biggest problem I'm seeing here, is that you're ignoring the H in HAB.<br /> <br /> The Hypothetical Bystander is hypothetical because they're not actually there. It's what that bystander would think if they were in the room with the mage. That's why you can conjure a business card or a small knife coincidentally (a HAB will believe you might have those in your pockets), but not a rocket launcher (because you can't fit that in your pockets). It doesn't matter if you do it away from where average people normally are, as that's negating the H part.<br /> <br /> The HAB is always watching you, just not as closely as the HOO. When your mage ducks into his workshop, the HAB follows. When the robot is created from nothing the HAB disbelieves and it's vulgar w/o witnesses, even if the HAB would be fooled by the workshop into believe in you a simple toy flying drone in one of your mage's cabinets when you actually used magic to create it inside the cabinet, because the HAB would be fooled by your mage rummaging around in a room where it is completely believable random bits of tech might be tucked in a drawer, bin, etc.<br /> <br /> The concealment has to be to the HAB that's standing there theoretically watching you, not to actual people passing by on the highway outside the quarry.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is cumbersome. If he's Average, he should not follow me into a private place. If I go to the bathroom, turn the lights off and do my Magick, is the fucker still there, disbelieving in the dark? This is weighty. You can do vulgar without witnesses and spend the paradox immediately. Then the storyteller has to dish out another paradox flaw. Your eyes glow red, you float an inch off the ground or whatever - just a vast list of nothing effects and three dice of bashing damage. I want paradox to be consequential and avoidable - emphasis on Actual witnesses and how many. As it stands, the difference in paradox points you get from doing vulgar Magick in front of a large crowd and taking fairly reasonable steps to create coincidence is not that much. If the HAB is going to wreck anything I try to do, why not go to the main intersection of town and materialize a giant statue of a porcupine? Going to get punished anyway. I certainly don't want my players to be punished for any little act of Magick when I have just promised that MAGE is fun. I will design my own paradox system in due time.<br /> <br /> Drawers, then.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1418137-quintessence-quarry-extracting-from-matter-coincidentally?p=1418342#post1418342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Robots are generally controlled by a mix of computers and biological inputs (I say only because there's some neat cow milking robots that the cows learn to operate instead of having humans do anything).<br /> <br /> Automation is constantly advancing, but we're still pretty far from completely automated work forces. Most &quot;autonomous&quot; mining equipment is more accurately remote controlled mining equipment because there's still an operator or two that get to be safely away from the highly dangerous activity. The robots are still doing a lot of computing on their own to let two operators replace a team of a dozen to two dozen workers, but they're not doing it without human input either.<br /> <br /> More importantly to this scenario: Matter and Prime alone can't generate computer code to have your mining robot programmed as you bring it into existence, and most mining operations use multiple automation based machines, not just one all-purpose mining robot so keeping to modern technology means building lots of different robots, not just one.</div> </div> </div> </div>A computer's hard drive requires Forces, because it runs on charges to store binary information. I'm already factoring in things that are not strictly Matter, including the software. There are expenses.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1418137-quintessence-quarry-extracting-from-matter-coincidentally?p=1418342#post1418342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unfortunately left up to the ST rather than having hard rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>I will go with mass over volume. The question of value as it relates to Paradigm is both open to abuse and interesting to ponder. As a personal opinion, I don't think gold is of any value. I know it has been the basis of national economies for thousands of years and other people believe that its rarity and immunity to corrosion make it valuable. But in terms of being able to do anything with it, gold is useless. It should not be valued as it is. This is part of my paradigm. I will just use myself as a hypothetical Mage character with the appropriate Spheres.<br /> <br /> If the cost of creating something is based on its &quot;value&quot; and that depends on paradigm and the yield from sacrificing is the same, there is a glitch. You can probably tell where this is going. I can create bricks of gold, because I don't see much use for the substance. Another Mage can sacrifice it for the value his paradigm assigns the gold. Assume they are a goldsmith who creates gem encrusted statues, reselling it for higher value. They can sac the gold for more quint than it took to create it. We can then exchange quintessence. To a Verbena, money may have much less value than active living biomass in nature. There's a differential to be exploited there too.<br /> <br /> There is still a glitch, even if you use the universal Consensus Paradigm, where the Syndicate controls the commodities market and everything has dollar value. No differential value between Mages' paradigms. Take the example of waste rock. There are a multitude of things it can be shaped into that give it value. I have crafts 3. I can reshape it with Matter 3 into a statue of an Etherite macguffin, then sacrifice it. Then, create even more mass of metal-poor rock (except for the silicon and magnesium that are almost always present). I am not actually going to allow this feedback loop in game.<br /> <br /> There is also differential value between Sleepers' possessions. Take an estate auction. Someone died and their things are being sold. I buy something that was special and important to the deceased that isn't worth a lot of money. I sac it for quint. If it has to be a living person, a foreclosure auction. If I can turn that quint into a large quantity of low-dollar-value material, reshape and sell it, I can keep subsidizing auction trips.<br /> <br /> Analysis?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1418137-quintessence-quarry-extracting-from-matter-coincidentally?p=1418342#post1418342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That presumes someone isn't trying to harvest the free floating quintessence in the local area like your plan relies on. While it is true the default is that there's plenty of free quintessence in the background of reality for mages not to worry about fueling patterns, your plan involves messing with that on a large scale. Also the number of successes you'd need to generate industrial mining amounts of rocks is high enough to get into auto-quintessence costs.</div> </div> </div> </div>A quintessence tug of war. There don't appear to be rules for that. Some more homebrew. I will make a session out of it. I'm already going with mining for mining's sake, selling to the market and supplying other Tradition Mages with raw materials.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1418137-quintessence-quarry-extracting-from-matter-coincidentally?p=1418342#post1418342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Possibly, but the plan you've outlined isn't efficient for this purpose. Matter 2 and Prime 2 will get you lots more Quintessence, but you need objects of significant enough value that destroying them is an actual sacrifice... which means you can't industrialize it... and stealing such objects from Sleepers is a dick move (but hey, lots of mages are assholes). The problems are when you try to turn this into an elaborate scheme that includes an actual front business.</div> </div> </div> </div>What problem arises from raiding foreclosure auctions, if I create a business for that purpose?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1418137-quintessence-quarry-extracting-from-matter-coincidentally?p=1418342#post1418342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Prime 1: Sense the quintessence in the first place, store more in you than your natural limit, damage yourself for quintessence, redirect quintessence into objects to bind them to your personal Pattern.<br /> Prime 2: Sacrifice objects for quintessence, redirect quintessence into Patterns to fuel them, redirect quintessence into existing objects to make them better.<br /> Prime 3: Sacrifice living things for quintessence, redirect quintessence between willing mages, redirect quintessence into living things to make them better, redirect quintessence directly from some sources to yourself.<br /> <br /> That's not &quot;can't do anything.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>There's also Body of Light - could allow the Time Mage to help realize my character's potential. I specified it's usefulness for getting quintessence. M20 says Prime 3 for Matter and no mention of the personal connection to the object. It immediately contradicts itself in the entry for Prime 4. How Do You Do That says Prime 4, has a chart for sacrificing animals and not a single example of what an object's yield might be.<br /> <br /> I would not have thought deeply about Wellsprings. I think focusing on the Verbena's music career and influencing the election could keep us in supply and move the story faster. Not too fast, though. There is also extracting from matter in Umbral Realms where paradox doesn't apply. Need an Ether Ship.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":26467,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","user":"HorizonParty2021","date":". 10-16-2020, 06:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-16T06:49:17-07:00","id":1418519,"title":"","content":"Honestly, given the number of times some form of &quot;house rules,&quot; has come up, I'm not sure how much you really expect any of us to be able to help. We don't know what house rules your using, and how they're going to impact the viability of any given strategy. If you're going nuts house ruling the game in lots of ways, house rule it to make what you want to work work. We can only effectively comment on what the plausibility of something is using the RAW, or help you with house rules if you ask specifically about a given rule and what you want to change about it and why..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-16T07:15:49-07:00","id":1418523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> ...Stuff about value = Quint...<br /> <br /> Analysis? </div> </div> </div>Well, that's certainly a good example of how there should be a rule abut this instead of just a vague conept. <hr />However, my analisis it's <i>also </i>that your hipotetical mage it's an evident attempt by a player to rig the system by being <i>insincere </i>about what the mage deems valuable.<br /> <br /> Why?<br /> <br /> Because you're taking pains to recover that gold that supposedly has so little value for your character...yet I don't see any qualms about making all that &quot;Oh, so Valuable for my Paradigm&quot; rock disappear.<br /> <br /> Valuable things are supposed to be...well..<u><b><i>valuable</i></b></u>. You can't have a theory saying rock it's totally more valuable that gold, but then crave all the gold while shedding no tears for the rock. I'mean, maybe your character it's crying on the inside for all that sacrifice....but, what can I say: The whole deal would be <i>very </i>suspicious to me.<br /> <br /> If I was your ST, you would have to give me a <i>really </i>good explanation about how your mages trade trough different perceptions about &quot;value&quot; to get the most of their sacrifices, if you want me to allow such shenanigans. If this &quot;market of value&quot; it's interesting enough I migth even allow it, but as presented it would face a serious case of &quot;the look&quot; - if you get what I mean. <hr /><br /> That being said: The fact that the presented &quot;&quot;&quot;system?&quot;&quot;&quot; it's way too vague (and, yes, prone to abuse) doesn't just disappear, I agree with you.<br /> <br /> I still think, however, that Value jives much more with how magick works in Mage than mass or any other thing, because I can trace a paralel of how Correspondence works trough &quot;connections&quot; rather than measurable distance.<br /> In mage, symbols and value are clearly very important things, even beyond that particular rote. The difference being that Correspondence has a table clearing many doubts about what a &quot;significative&quot; connection may be. Sacrifice doesn't","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-16T18:19:09-07:00","id":1418621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1418137-quintessence-quarry-extracting-from-matter-coincidentally?p=1418519#post1418519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, given the number of times some form of &quot;house rules,&quot; has come up, I'm not sure how much you really expect any of us to be able to help. We don't know what house rules your using, and how they're going to impact the viability of any given strategy. If you're going nuts house ruling the game in lots of ways, house rule it to make what you want to work work. We can only effectively comment on what the plausibility of something is using the RAW, or help you with house rules if you ask specifically about a given rule and what you want to change about it and why..</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1418137-quintessence-quarry-extracting-from-matter-coincidentally#post1418137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a storyteller, would this work in your chronicle?</div> </div> </div> </div>To clarify the Meaning of the question, it does not exclude storytellers who use their own homebrew or interpret Magick rules less strictly. There are a significant number of storytellers with homebrew whose ideas are represented in the other posts on this forum.<br /> <br /> The Intention of asking the question this is to obtain a broad sample from storytellers based on how they actually play. It's obviously important to engage with feedback with STs who follow RAW more strictly, because it ensures that the greatest number of STs and players would find the story believable. <br /> <br /> There are only two homebrew items that I have mentioned. Alternative Conjunctional Magick does not change the question, because it is only my character who is described building the quarrying facility. <br /> <br /> Alternative Paradox was an idea that I had, but was not forced to develop in a hurry, because I properly conveyed to my players the dangers of doing vulgar Magick, not only minor backlash, but its potential to attract the attention of the Technocracy. They avoid doing vulgar magick enough that I can use the old paradox flaws and &quot;escape from this micro-realm&quot; diversions without running out of ideas. <br /> <br /> When discussing RAW, our discussion skipped over something. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1418137-quintessence-quarry-extracting-from-matter-coincidentally#post1418137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How Do You Do That, p45, right column, under heading: Conjuring Material Forms,<br /> &quot;For obvious reasons, this sort of thing tends to be vulgar Magick, although a sufficient level of concealment can make it seem coincidental.&quot; It then refers to the Axis of Coincidence chart M20,p533-534, which emphasizes Hypothetical Average Bystander (HAB) and Process Based Determinism (PBD). What would the average person believe? How do you do it?</div> </div> </div> </div>The direct quote from How Do You Do That, published more recently than M20 Core, refers to a sufficient level of concealment. Before we even get to the Axis of Coincidence, &quot;sufficient level&quot; has to be examined. There are two things being proposed, drawers versus an entire infrastructure building intended to make the production pass under the masses' incredulity.<br /> <br /> The Mage who clears out his garage and gets some storage cabinets from Walmart is supposedly better protected from paradox, because the HAB can't squeeze himself inside the drawers. If the drawers belong to the Mage and he's the only one who uses the garage, the HAB knows he didn't put anything in the drawers, because he follows the Mage at all times. Is &quot;HAB&quot; a part time position, filled by different HABs working in shifts? Can a Mage do vulgar magick in the bathroom? If not, how &quot;Average&quot; is this bystander, psychologically speaking?<br /> <br /> The Consensus established by the Technocracy assumes that the survivability nearly eight billion Sleepers depends on increasing production. The Consensus is fueled by Sleepers. Paradox is an enforcement agent that rests on eight billion hungry, greedy Sleepers. Paradox punishes someone who works within the consensus to improve the economy? The Mage's own greed is not a sin in the eyes of Paradox. The Market Consensus rests on the Syndicate's ideas about what is good for the masses. <br /> <br /> Consider an opposite scenario. A Hit Mark, Biomechanic Mage attacks a crowd of Sleepers with vulgar Hyper-tech Magick (They are activists whose protest threatens a construct's operation, let's say, and he's in Jhor). In this instance, any Mage in the area gets a temporary reprieve, allowing him to use vulgar Magick only against the attacker to stop the massacre. Hostile Umbrood busting the Gauntlet - same thing. Can we not draw conclusions about when Paradox punishes the Mage from the instances in which it allows vulgar magick?<br /> <br /> I am incorporating ideas presented in the replies into my chronicle. I think the questions I just posed are worth reflection for anyone interested in improving player experience. Giving players a chance (as well as structured rules) is what brings people back to the table - or the podcast. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-16T19:34:25-07:00","id":1418626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1418137-quintessence-quarry-extracting-from-matter-coincidentally?p=1418621#post1418621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Mage who clears out his garage and gets some storage cabinets from Walmart is supposedly better protected from paradox, because the HAB can't squeeze himself inside the drawers. If the drawers belong to the Mage and he's the only one who uses the garage, the HAB knows he didn't put anything in the drawers, because he follows the Mage at all times. Is &quot;HAB&quot; a part time position, filled by different HABs working in shifts? Can a Mage do vulgar magick in the bathroom? If not, how &quot;Average&quot; is this bystander, psychologically speaking?</div> </div> </div> </div>HAB doesn't have any psychology because it's not a person. The Observer it's not *someone*, it's not even *anyone*.<br /> <br /> The spirit of the theory it's to provide a more concrete alternative for the <i>very </i>vague question of Mage that's the RAW way to determine (from 1e to M20) if something it's Vulgar. That question is: <b>Is this feat something that would be regarded as <i>impossible</i>?</b><br /> <br /> HAB interprets this question as<i> &quot;it's Vulgar if your mage it's doing something that would be regarded as impossible by an average person that's watching&quot;. </i><br /> <br /> That isn't propper to follow you into the bathroom doesn't enter into the equation. HAP it's allways watching you. The difference from the more strict observer it's just that, as an observer, has the perspective of a bystander that doesn't interact with the scene, nor possess superhuman senses.<br /> <br /> As a &quot;hipotetical&quot;, the observer it's always in the scene unless it would be impossible for an average human. But as a bystander, the observer doesn't have a particularly advantageous view of the scene. That's why it's said that it can't see what do you have in your pockets, it doesn't have X-Ray vision, and can't open your pockets to see what's there <hr /><br /> Again: HAB it's not a person, it doesn't have a mind, nor occupies any space.<i> HAB it's a question: <b>&quot;what if someone was watching me?&quot;</b></i>.<br /> That's what the observer is.<br /> <br /> If it's creepy to think so while you're in the bathroom doing your magick, well, too bad<br /> (srly: it's not like people never forgets to knock before entering a bathroom :P)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 10-16-2020, 10:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-16T19:49:20-07:00","id":1418627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1418137-quintessence-quarry-extracting-from-matter-coincidentally?p=1418523#post1418523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, that's certainly a good example of how there should be a rule abut this instead of just a vague conept. <hr />However, my analisis it's <i>also </i>that your hipotetical mage it's an evident attempt by a player to rig the system by being <i>insincere </i>about what the mage deems valuable.<br /> <br /> Why?<br /> <br /> Because you're taking pains to recover that gold that supposedly has so little value for your character...yet I don't see any qualms about making all that &quot;Oh, so Valuable for my Paradigm&quot; rock disappear.<br /> <br /> Valuable things are supposed to be...well..<u><b><i>valuable</i></b></u>. You can't have a theory saying rock it's totally more valuable that gold, but then crave all the gold while shedding no tears for the rock. I'mean, maybe your character it's crying on the inside for all that sacrifice....but, what can I say: The whole deal would be <i>very </i>suspicious to me.<br /> <br /> If I was your ST, you would have to give me a <i>really </i>good explanation about how your mages trade trough different perceptions about &quot;value&quot; to get the most of their sacrifices, if you want me to allow such shenanigans. If this &quot;market of value&quot; it's interesting enough I migth even allow it, but as presented it would face a serious case of &quot;the look&quot; - if you get what I mean. <hr /><br /> That being said: The fact that the presented &quot;&quot;&quot;system?&quot;&quot;&quot; it's way too vague (and, yes, prone to abuse) doesn't just disappear, I agree with you.</div> </div> </div> </div>If, as a player, I wanted to use this feedback loop, my character would also have Scientific Mystic/Technogasi merit and lots of occult, science, esoterica, cosmology. He would involve Mages with different paradigms, having each play a small role in the exchange without telling them the totality of what he was doing. That way, none of them have any doubt in what they are doing.<br /> <br /> There is even a way in which this could be included in a chronicle, as a Storyteller, without it being a consequence-free endeavor. The Syndicate's Enforcement methodology has a subgroup called InSpectres, who are tasked with infiltrating Chantries. So, a Syndicate spy with all the merits and abilities from the first example has a Tradition identity crafted for him. He approaches individual Mages with different paradigms and involves them in exchanges that facilitate the feedback loop. When the targets compare stories, they begin to figure out how their differential value of materials is being exploited. If they continue to participate after knowing the feedback loop is happening, it can have a variety of consequences.<br /> <br /> It may undermine each mage's own paradigm, making him susceptible to recruitment by outside Technocrats. The spy relays this information back to his construct. They start to develop Quiet. The quintessence each gained over time is suddenly all drained away from them at an inopportune moment.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> QUOTE=Aleph;n1418523]I still think, however, that Value jives much more with how magick works in Mage than mass or any other thing, because I can trace a paralel of how Correspondence works trough &quot;connections&quot; rather than measurable distance.<br /> In mage, symbols and value are clearly very important things, even beyond that particular rote. The difference being that Correspondence has a table clearing many doubts about what a &quot;significative&quot; connection may be. Sacrifice doesn't[/QUOTE]<br /> <br /> A good produced in large quantity, locally, has less value than in a place where is is scarce. A place that has poor transport infrastructure could be a Reality Zone with a different value for imported goods. They may treasure any imported good they can get or place greater value on the undeveloped natural spaces - the animal biomass that a forest generates.<br /> <br /> Character Concept: An altruistic entrepreneur concerned for the small national economy of his country. The country is in debt and the Syndicate is waiting to install an actual technocracy to run the country after an expected collapse. The national currency is predicted to fall, relative to the price of gold. He has Time 2, Matter 1, Prime 3. In the chronicle, he has time to raise his Matter and Prime Spheres to the required level to do more things. He rides the gold market using Time and invests in a local gold mining company. He accumulates a physical store of gold. When the national currency drops sharply, instead of selling the gold, he sacrifices it for quint. He enlists other Mages to intervene in the fate of the country, in exchange for quint. The gold mining company is saved from being cut off from the world market and carries on operating. Adding Correspondence, a Cabal could obtain goods from distant parts of the world at local prices. With Time, there is a symbolic value for antiques and ancient artifacts. Only a mater of finding them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":26467,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","user":"HorizonParty2021","date":". 10-17-2020, 05:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}